% Regression guard for the pitchof_b() global-buffer-overflow (store.c).
% Under a detune temperament (%%temperament, TEMPERDT), a note's semitone
% offset p -- scale[note] plus the accidental -- can leave the range 0..11:
% ^b gives 11 + 1 = 12 and _c gives 0 - 1 = -1.  That value used to index the
% twelve-element temperament_dt[] array directly, reading out of bounds.  The
% lookup now folds p to a pitch class (p mod 12), so B# takes C's detune and
% Cb takes B's, while the emitted pitch still uses the raw p.  Built with the
% sanitize preset against the pre-fix code this input aborts in pitchof_b, so
% it is a real regression guard and not just an output pin.
X:1
T:Detune accidental bounds
C:abc2midi test
M:4/4
L:1/4
K:C
%%temperament +00 -06 -04 -02 -08 +02 -08 -02 -04 -06 +00 -10
^b _c ^b _c |
